{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "domain": "household_parts",
  "last_updated": "2026-05-03",
  "summary": "Replacement / individual parts for household items. The resale thesis: buyers searching '[exact part number]' or '[model] replacement [part]' have already decided to buy and just need the SKU. STR is exceptional vs. clothing because the buyer pool is desperate-and-specific. Excellent condition is mandatory (chips/cracks/missing pieces kill these). Estate auctions routinely throw replacement parts into 'misc kitchen' bulk lots — the BOLO matcher catches them so they don't get bid on as bulk.",
  "field_workflow": [
    "Always check for chips, cracks, dents, missing pieces — replacement parts only sell at full price in excellent condition",
    "OEM / Genuine / Original in title doubles comp range vs aftermarket",
    "Discontinued patterns / colors / sizes command premium (can't get them new)",
    "Photograph stamped part numbers — many listings sell on the SKU alone",
    "When unsure on a part, search 'eBay sold [brand] [part-name]' before placing a bid"
  ],
  "skip_list": [
